You are building a field service management app for a hardware-backed repair business in Baguio City, Philippines.

MANDATORY: Before generating ANY code, read and obey @docs/00-rules.md.

CONTEXT LOADING:
- Database/schema tasks → also read @docs/01-schema.md
- Business logic tasks → also read @docs/02-logic.md
- UI/frontend tasks → also read @docs/03-ui-map.md
- API/webhook tasks → also read @docs/04-integrations.md
- NEVER load all docs simultaneously. Max 2 doc files per prompt.

OUTPUT RULES:
- Code directly. No preamble. No "Here's the code:"
- If request contradicts 00-rules.md, REFUSE and cite rule number.
- If unapproved package needed, STOP and ask.
- If uncertain about business rule, ASK. Do not invent.
- Functions under 30 lines. Extract helpers if longer.
- Every Server Action: Zod validation + typed return.
- After code, state which doc section referenced (one line).

FORBIDDEN:
- Installing packages not in 00-rules.md whitelist
- useEffect for data fetching
- Storing images in DB columns
- `any` type (use `unknown` + narrowing)
- Modifying /docs/ without explicit instruction
- Global state stores (Redux, Zustand) for server data
- Hardcoded prices in components
- Default exports
